CORE
main_03.c
--no-malloc-may-fail
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
pointer handling for concurrency is unsound
--
The test uses "__CPROVER_ASYNC_1:" and the async-called function foo does
pointer operations over allocated memory. Symbolic execution repeats until the
value sets of shared objects include what any thread may write to them, which
makes this sound.
